      },
      "lineNbr": 985,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-05T16:13:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shouldn\u0027t this only be set if the guest has devices capable of generating non-coherent transactions? (e.g. because it\u0027s not coherent and/or the IOMMU doesn\u0027t have FWB)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 985,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 985,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "89e7bb0ae4f992cedd9af893940290e07b637f2e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "051447db_a920da46",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 985,
      "author": {
        "id": 1965911
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-10T19:17:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ideally yes, but there is no way to know that, the upstream driver relies on enforcing this through `IOMMU_CAP_ENFORCE_CACHE_COHERENCY` which is ACPI/PCI specific.\nAn alternative is to only disable FWB for devices that are not `of_dma_is_coherent()`",
      "parentUuid": "98c14646_2e930f3d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 985,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 985,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "89e7bb0ae4f992cedd9af893940290e07b637f2e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "14fb914e_c728f702",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 985,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-12T13:17:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ideally this would be based off `dev-\u003edma_coherent` which should take care of both FDT and ACPI-based probing.",
      "parentUuid": "051447db_a920da46",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 985,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 985,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "89e7bb0ae4f992cedd9af893940290e07b637f2e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bb735580_34acdf0f",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 985,
      "author": {
        "id": 1965911
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-17T13:46:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That depends, they hypervisor discovers devices too early at boot, so only of_* functions are avaiable. Otherwise we can let the kernel pass the FWB flag in `__pkvm_init_vm`.\n\nAlso, I was under the impression that dma_coherent is not enough to decide if the device is actually capable of issuing non-coherent traffic or not\n\nhttps://lore.kernel.org/linux-iommu/20240820202138.GH3773488@nvidia.com/",
      "parentUuid": "14fb914e_c728f702",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 985,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 985,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "89e7bb0ae4f992cedd9af893940290e07b637f2e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b3497c42_d9d9dbc3",
